{
 "_comment": "The public identity of every plugin module tracker-ff 1.3.0 ships, and the repository that builds it. No module source is in this repository: the synth engines are built in tracker-engines-os (public, the OpenTracker 3.x module engines) and tracker-engines (private, our own engines), the master inserts in tracker-effects-os (public, the OpenTracker fx ports) and tracker-effects (private, our own inserts). engines/external.lock.json pins a release of each repository (tag, commit, sha256 of every published file), engines/check_modules.py verify-external checks the published files against the rows here. Engine rows: id = file name (<id>.plg, <id>.plgi, <id>.wasm, <id>.json), name = the descriptor name (engine_list.h), stored, patch, type = the numbers of the engine (plug_abi.h PLUG_SYNTH_MANIFEST, engine_list.h), version = the .plg header version, logo = the card logo text. Insert rows: plug_id and version of the .plg header. visibility and repo: where the source lives (repos lists them). licence: what the published files carry, the module repository ships the texts. A module repository must not change these numbers: a new engine gets its row here (and its engine_list.h entry) first. optional: a row with an optional group is only built, checked and shipped when the group is switched on (--with GROUP). No row has one in 1.3.0. The firmware image does not change: a plugin engine brings its own stored, patch and type numbers, the host takes any free ones (engine_list.h lists the built-in engines only, and is a pinned SDK header).",
